THIRD-PARTY NOTICES
===================

This project's demonstration game "Zork1" (the sources under `Sources/Zork1/`)
is an original Swift re-implementation of the interactive-fiction classic
*Zork I: The Great Underground Empire*.

Zork I was written by Marc Blank, Dave Lebling, Bruce Daniels, and Tim Anderson,
and published by Infocom in 1980.


Reproduced textual content
--------------------------

The room descriptions, object descriptions, and player-facing messages in
`Sources/Zork1/` — and the Zork I/II/III columns of the reference documents under
`docs/games/` — reproduce text from the original Zork source code. That text was
taken from the publicly available source-code collections published at:

    https://github.com/historicalsource/zork1
    https://github.com/historicalsource/zork2
    https://github.com/historicalsource/zork3

Those three repositories were open-sourced in November 2025 by Microsoft's Open
Source Programs Office with Team Xbox and Activision, in collaboration with Jason
Scott of the Internet Archive. Note that the sibling repository
`historicalsource/zork` (an Infocom-era mainframe port) was NOT part of that
release and is not relied on here.

