Two limits on the above, recorded so a later pass does not have to rediscover them
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. The MITDDC grant covers the 1977 and 1978 versions it published. The version
   this project reconstructs is the final MDL, dated 1981-07-22, which reached the
   public through Bob Supnik's 2003 release rather than through MITDDC, and for
   which no comparable grant has been located.

   Accordingly, the 1981 source is consulted for STRUCTURE — map topology, exit
   tables, point values, object properties, puzzle logic — and reproduced TEXT is
   taken only from clearly granted sources: the Zork I/II/III ZIL above, and the
   MITDDC MDL versions. Where a room or object exists only in the 1981 source and
   in neither granted body, its prose is written fresh for this project and the
   divergence is recorded in FIDELITY.md.

   In practice this gap is narrow: the content present in 1981 but absent from the
   1978 MDL is almost entirely the Bank of Zork, the mirror box, and the Endgame,
   all three of which the trilogy preserved — Zork III keeps even the mainframe's
   own room identifiers for the Endgame.

2. https://github.com/heasm66/mdlzork, which hosts the runnable reconstructions of
   each MDL version, states no license for its own reconstruction and patching
   work. It is used here only to identify versions and to run the original for
   behavioural reference. Nothing is reproduced from it.


Purpose
-------

Like the archive it draws from, this material is included for education,
discussion, and historical work — allowing researchers and students to study how
these interactive-fiction games were made and how the system dealt with input and
processing. It is offered in that same spirit of preservation and study.
